\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Stronger On US CPI Data, Ctrl Bk Dlr Auction  \b0\par\par\uc2 341 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2005\par 22:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real closed stronger Friday, after softer-than-expected core inflation data were released in the U.S., and after Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  entered the market for a fourth time this week, purchasing dollars.  \par \par \uc2 The real closed at 2.246 per dollar, stronger than Thursday's close at BRL2.257 to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday reacted to both external and domestic news Friday, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 While headline consumer price inflation in the U.S. was up 1.2% in September, the core number - stripped of energy and food prices - was up 0.1%, while economists had expected a rise of 0.2%.  \par \par \uc2 A positive reaction by markets abroad to the U.S. CPI figure helped Brazil's real, traders said. A more benign U.S. inflation reading diminishes the need for further interest rate increases in the U.S. that would diminish the spread between U.S. rates and Brazilian rates, luring out funds from Brazil to the U.S.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar also lost ground against major world \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday, such as the euro and the yen, helping the real to strengthen further.  \par \par \uc2 An \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy U.S. dollars at an auction early Friday afternoon for BRL2.254 to the dollar, may also have boosted the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real was trading at BRL2.2541 to the dollar before the bank called the auction at 1507 GMT. The real traded slightly stronger, at BRL2.252 to the dollar, shortly after the auction.  \par \par \uc2 It was the fourth time this week that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought dollars from the market, continuing a string of purchases aimed at beefing up the country's foreign reserves.  \par \par \uc2 The bank also bought dollars on Monday, Tuesday, and Thursday. Brazil's financial markets were closed Wednesday for a holiday.  \par \par \uc2 -By Bernd Radowitz, Dow Jones Newswires; (55 21) 3288 5004; bernd.radowitz@dowjones.com [ 14-10-05 2001GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1156 1843  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020051014e1ae000vj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
