\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Closes Weaker After Ctrl Bank  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 436 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Oktober 2005\par 22:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2005, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.    \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Oct 13, 2005 (DJCS via Comtex) --  \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real closed weaker against the U.S. dollar Thursday in the wake of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's third auction this week to purchase dollars from the market.  \par \par \uc2 The real closed at BRL2.257 to the dollar, down from Tuesday's close of BRL2.234. Brazilian financial markets were closed Wednesday for a holiday.  \par \par \uc2 At 1535 GMT, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  called an auction to purchase dollars from the market, following similar moves on Monday and Tuesday. The bank bought dollars at BRL2.260. The real traded slightly weaker at BRL2.261 shortly after the auction, but reversed course and strengthened toward the close.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's purchase Thursday followed a series dollar buying by the bank that began last week. The bank had said it would begin to enter the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in an effort to beef up Brazil's foreign reserves.  \par \par \uc2 The real also was pressured by continued expectations of interest rate hikes in the U.S., analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 The release Tuesday of minutes from the U.S. Federal Reserve's recent meeting and comments Wednesday by Fed Chairman Alan Greenspan signaled that the U.S. monetary body would likely continue its recent monetary tightening cycle. The rate hikes are aimed at warding off inflationary pressures.  \par \par \uc2 The Federal Open Market Committee, the U.S. Federal Reserve's rate-setting body, next meets Nov. 1.  \par \par \uc2 In addition, the real suffered with the discovery of foot-and-mouth disease on a farm in Mato Grosso do Sul state, the heart of Brazil's beef-producing region, analysts said. Discovery of the outbreak caused the European Union and Russia to ban some imports of Brazilian beef.  \par \par \uc2 Because the state produces up to 50% of Brazil's world-leading beef exports, current shipments of up to $3 billion per year could be slashed significantly in the fourth quarter of 2005 and, perhaps, all of 2006.  \par \par \uc2 Strong Brazilian exports have been a primary factor in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength in 2005. The real has gained 18% against the U.S. dollar so far this year.  \par \par \uc2 The country's risk spread against U.S. Treasurys also widened Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 At 1943 GMT, the spread as measured by the J.P. Morgan Emerging Markets Bond Index Plus widened 8 basis points to 388 basis points over U.S. Treasurys. Brazil's benchmark 2040 bond was down 0.550 at 117.900.  \par \par \uc2 -By Jeff Fick, Dow Jones Newswires; (55 11) 3145-1481; jeff.fick@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires  \par \par \uc2 10-13-05 1546ET  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020051013e1ad006pu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
