\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Soy - Market seen recovering from 8-mth low  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Roberto Samora  \par \uc2 566 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Oktober 2005\par 22:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Brazil, Oct 13 (Reuters) - Brazilian soybean prices are expected to recover from an eight-month low if Chicago consolidates strong gains this week and the dollar strengthens against the real, traders said on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Benchmark Chicago futures jumped to a one-month high on Wednesday on the back of a smaller-than-expected monthly government U.S. crop estimate.  \par \par \uc2 In a bid to weaken the real which is at multiyear highs against the dollar, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  seven times since early last week to buy the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Despite the bank's purchases, the dollar was lower on Thursday than a week ago, settling at around 2.258 reais, vs. 2.269 reais on Oct. 5 and around 2.90 reais a year ago.  \par \par \uc2 "Domestic soy prices have been falling due to the firm real and weak world prices," said analyst Fernando Muraro at Agencia Rural, adding, "There's a lot of soy and little local demand."  \par \par \uc2 Muraro estimated that about 20 percent of the 2005 crop was unsold and that demand had been reduced by the recent closures of soybean crushing plants by Archer Daniels Midland in Paranagau and by Bunge in Cuiaba.  \par \par \uc2 On Monday, a 60-kg bag of soybeans was quoted at 23.50 reais in Rondonopolis, Mato Grosso state, the lowest level since Feb. 8, 2005. Prices at the main grains export port of Paranagua were near the year's low at 29 reais per bag.  \par \par \uc2 Premiums for new crop deliveries next year, however, have risen. March premiums rose to 25/30 cents over Chicago compared with 20/25 cents last week. April-May premiums were higher at 11/15 cents over compared with 7/12 over last week.  \par \par \uc2 "The (Brazilian) market should react (to Chicago) but it doesn't mean a new trend," said Steve Cachia, analyst at Cerealpar in Curitiba, Parana state.  \par \par \uc2 He added that Brazilian prices had taken an unusual fall during the inter-harvest period, due mainly to the weakness of the dollar against the real.  \par \par \uc2 Agencia Rural's Muraro said that the United States was harvesting for the second successive year a huge crop of more than 80 million tonnes.  \par \par \uc2 South America is starting to sow its new soybean crop which is expected to total 105 million tonnes, Muraro said, estimating Brazilian output at 57 million tonnes, Argentine at 41 million and Paraguay, Bolivia and Uruguay a combined 7 million tonnes.  \par \par \uc2 Following is a domestic price table for Oct. 5 from grain centers in key soybean states. Prices are in reais.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par STATE GRAIN         Soybeans      Meal          Oil\par CENTERS            /60-kg bag    /tonne        /tonne\par                           (47 pct protein)\par -----------------------------------------------------------\par Barreiras (BA)      24.80        415              1350\par Rio Verde (GO)      24.850       430              1300\par Cuiaba (MT)         22.50        400              1050\par Rondonopolis (MT)   24.50        430              1200\par Campo Mourao (PR)   28.00        470              1250\par Cascavel (PR)       28.30        460              1250\par Maringa (PR)        27.50        470              1065\par Ponta Grossa (PR)   30.00        500                --\par Passo Fundo (RS)    27.00        500              1400\par Chapeco (SC)        28.00        530              1150\par Orlandia (SP)       27.00        500              1120\par Balsas (MA)         23.00         -                 --\par Sorriso (MT)        21.40 