\par\par \b \uc2 ADR Report-ADRs buoyed by oil and Brazilian shares  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Emily Chasan  \par \uc2 479 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2005\par 19:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Oct 7 (Reuters) - Overseas shares traded in the United States rose on Friday, as a rebound in oil prices lifted oil companies' American Depositary Receipts and U.S.-listed stocks of Brazilian companies rose sharply as inflation appeared to be getting under control there.  \par \par \uc2 However, better-than-expected U.S. job data kept the market in check as investors believe that meant another interest-rate hike would be almost certain.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of New York's index of leading ADRs <.BKADR> was up 0.4 percent at a time when the 30-share Dow Jones industrial average <.DJI> was up 0.2 percent at 10,304.64.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S.-listed shares of Brazilian companies soared on Friday as \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign- exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by buying dollars for the fourth time this week.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be a boon to \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's exporters as its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar purchases help control inflation and the Brazilian real has been near four-year-highs. Controlling inflation could help exporters keep foreign sales from slowing.  \par \par \uc2 Shares of Brazilian oil producer Petrobras climbed 5.5 percent to $64.76, while shares of Brazilian bank Unibanco advanced 4.6 percent to $50.82.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of New York's index of leading Latin American ADRs <.BKLA> rose 3.3 percent to 186.39.  \par \par \uc2 Shares of Chilean power company Enersis jumped 4.7 percent to $12.06 after it said it would merge Chilectra, Chile's top power distributor, with its Elesur unit in a deal that could help it save $187 million in coming years. Enersis holds a majority stake in Chilectra.  \par \par \uc2 Oil companies' shares also gained some ground as U.S. crude oil futures prices stayed above $61 a barrel on Friday. Royal Dutch Shell shares rose 0.3 percent to $62.90.  \par \par \uc2 On the New York Mercantile Exchange, crude oil for November delivery rose as high as $61.90 a barrel, up from Thursday's close, and up sharply from a two-month low of $60.70 hit on Thursday. By Friday afternoon, though, NYMEX November crude was down 6 cents at $61.30.  \par \par \uc2 But shares of European and Asian companies made mostly muted gains in U.S. trading on Friday, as investors fretted over hawkish comments this week from officials of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the U.S. Federal Reserve. Comments from officials this week suggested that further monetary tightening would be necessary to contain inflationary pressures.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of New York's index of leading European ADRs <.BKEUR> was up 0.1 percent at 131.16, while its index of leading Asian ADRs <.BKAS> was up 1.1 percent at 120.84.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-STOCKS-ADRS|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|U|UKI|J|Z|RNP|DNP|PCO  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051007e1a7001k9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
47
