o stem the rise in the real, saying they are losing competitiveness.  \par \par \uc2 Exports, however, continue to boom. Brazil's foreign trade surplus in the year through September reached $32.67 billion, nearing 2004's full-year surplus of $34 billion. Analysts estimate the country will attain a trade surplus of $41 billion this year.  \par \par \uc2 Brazilian motor vehicle exports, however, fell 4.1 in September from the previous month. Carmakers have long complained that the current strength of the real renders their exports unprofitable.  \par \par \uc2 -By Bernd Radowitz, Dow Jones Newswires; (55 21) 3288 5004; bernd.radowitz@dowjones.com [ 06-10-05 1437GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument EM00000020051006e1a600012\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
