\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Closes Weaker After Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 324 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Oktober 2005\par 21:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real closed weaker against the U.S. dollar Wednesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  entered the market for a third day, buying the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The real closed at BRL2.268 to the dollar, 0.3% weaker than Tuesday's close of BRL2.261.  \par \par \uc2 Late Wednesday morning the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought U.S. dollars from the market at a rate of BRL2.272 per dollar, the bank said. The dollars were acquired at an auction, but the bank didn't disclose the volume of its purchases.  \par \par \uc2 The real was trading at BRL2.276 shortly after the auction, weaker than the BRL2.274 at which it traded shortly before the auction was announced. However, the real strengthened from that level to its close.  \par \par \uc2 The bank already had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market both on Monday and Tuesday. According to market participants, the bank bought small lots of dollars from institutions Monday, while making larger purchases on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Before the current round of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last entered the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on March 16.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't try to impose a ceiling for the real through its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , former \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Director Luiz Fernando Figueiredo was quoted as saying on the Agencia Estado newswire. Instead, he said, it was trying to prop up Brazil's foreign reserves - an explanation also given by \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Henrique Meirelles during \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier this year.  \par \par \uc2 However, said Figueiredo, without the bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real would already trade stronger than BRL2.00 per dollar. Figueiredo now works at the brokerage Maua Investimentos.  \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real has gained 17% against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year amid strong dollar inflows from exporting businesses and positive market sentiment toward Brazil's macroeconomic fundamentals.  \par \par \uc2 -By Bernd Radowitz, Dow Jones Newswires; 5521-3288-5004; bernd.radowitz@dowjones.com [ 05-10-05 1957GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1156 1843  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020051005e1a5000xo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
