\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Opens Weaker As Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Expected  \b0\par\par\uc2 238 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Oktober 2005\par 15:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real opened weaker against the U.S. dollar Wednesday amid expectations the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may enter the market again to buy the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The real opened at BRL2.278, weaker from Tuesday's close at BRL2.261 per dollar. The real then, however, strengthened to BRL2.273 in early morning trading until 1309 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market both on Monday and Tuesday, supposedly to buy dollars to increase Brazil's foreign reserves, but most traders think the bank is trying to prop up the real, and impede it from strengthening further.  \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year through early Wednesday has gained almost 17% against the greenback.  \par \par \uc2 After the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  early Tuesday bought dollars at BRL2.240 per dollar, the real fell steadily through the afternoon.  \par \par \uc2 It was unclear, however, how many dollars the bank bought. Tuesday marked the second day in a row of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  through an auction system.  \par \par \uc2 This week's auctions were the first at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars since March.  \par \par \uc2 If the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  abstains from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, the real could rebound Wednesday amid continued strong inflows of exporter dollars.  \par \par \uc2 -By Bernd Radowitz, Dow Jones Newswires; 5521-3288-5004; bernd.radowitz@dowjones.com [ 05-10-05 1319GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1156 1843  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020051005e1a5000ob\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
