\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  stocks end down;  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  weakens real  \b0\par\par\uc2 379 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Oktober 2005\par 15:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Oct 4 (Reuters) - Brazil's real weakened sharply on Tuesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars for the second straight day, while stocks fell after breaking 32,000 for the first time early in the session.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rebuild scant foreign reserves and, indirectly, weaken the real <BRBY> from a four-year high to help exporters.  \par \par \uc2 The real lost 1.35 percent to end at 2.26 a U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 After a six-month hiatus, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to make more \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the days ahead as inflation, which normally accelerates when the real weakens, is firmly under control.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely be doing this often from now on. So long as dollar inflows are positive it will step in to soak them up," a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at a Brazilian brokerage in Rio de Janeiro said.  \par \par \uc2 Some said the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , part of a broader government program to boost hard reserves and attain investment grade status, would need to be aggressive to absorb heavy dollar inflows.  \par \par \uc2 "Overseas corporate bond sales this year are 40 percent higher than last year and exports are very strong," the director of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a Brazilian national bank said.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Brazil's Bovespa <.BVSP> lost ground after breaking the latest in a string of records and traders said it could slip even more after gaining some 12 percent last month.  \par \par \uc2 The stock index finished 1.8 percent down at 31,283. Most stocks fell and blue chip Petrobras slumped 3.89 percent to 34.60 reais on tumbling world oil prices.  \par \par \uc2 Tuesday's sell-offs were the sharpest in several weeks and cut into months of gains.  \par \par \uc2 Brazilian assets prices have rallied during the past several months on sound economic fundamentals that have resisted a bribes scandal that has weakened President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva's administration.  \par \par \uc2 Investors fleeing low yields in the United States and Europe have also bought Brazilian bonds to gain exposure to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's benchmark interest rate of 19.5 percent.  \par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Nathalia Ferreira and Juliana Siqueira)  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-BRAZIL (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|D|M|E|RBN|U|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051004e1a400159\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
