\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Closes Weaker After  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 276 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Oktober 2005\par 21:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real closed weaker against the U.S. dollar Tuesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  entered the market to buy the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The real closed at BRL2.261 per dollar, down from the Monday close of BRL2.230.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  early in trading. The bank bought dollars at BRL2.240 per dollar, and the real fell steadily through the afternoon.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the bank bought modest volumes of dollars. However, Tuesday marked the second day in a row of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  through an auction system.  \par \par \uc2 This week's auctions were the first at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars since March.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the emerging pattern of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could mean the government is ready to establish a ceiling for the real, which has gained more than 18% against the dollar so far this year. A policy of supporting the dollar against the real would help to assure continued robust exports in 2006, according to analysts.  \par \par \uc2 Another reason for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases of dollars would be to beef up foreign reserves. As of Thursday, foreign reserves stood at $57.04 billion, less than one year's imports of about $75 billion.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the real could rebound Wednesday on exporter and investor inflows. Brazil posted a September foreign trade surplus of $4.329 billion. Meanwhile, Votorantim Bank and Gerdau Steel later this week will bring in some $400 million in proceeds from bond issues.  \par \par \uc2 -By Tom Murphy, Dow Jones Newswires; 5511-3145-1481; brazil@dowjones.com [ 04-10-05 1952GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1156 1843  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020051004e1a4000u7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
