\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil currency \highlight\uc2  gains despite  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  threat  \b0\par\par\uc2 394 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 September 2005\par 17:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Sept 29 (Reuters) - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened to a fresh four-year high on Thursday as heavy dollar inflows offset comments from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that it could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  "at any time" to stop the rally.  \par \par \uc2 At the Sao Paulo Stock Exchange, the benchmark Bovespa <.BVSP> index dipped 0.35 percent to end at 31,208.8 points after closing at a record high on Wednesday, the latest set during the past week.  \par \par \uc2 The real <BRBY> rose 0.98 percent to end at 2.213 per dollar, its strongest finish since May 2001.  \par \par \uc2 It weakened briefly after \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Economic Policy Director Afonso Bevilaqua reiterated the bank could resume dollar purchases halted in March under a program to rebuild foreign reserves and make Brazil more resistant to financial shocks.  \par \par \uc2 But he did not promise the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would return to the market or say when it might resume buying dollars. As a result, the real recovered quickly.  \par \par \uc2 Bevilaqua said that under the program the government has no preferred price for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and would only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to correct imbalances in a market awash with dollars.  \par \par \uc2 Inflows are heavy as exporters repatriate sales dollars, companies bring back proceeds from bonds sold overseas and high domestic interest rates lure foreign investors fleeing low yield in the United States and Europe.  \par \par \uc2 "With these high interest rates, everyone is buying the real," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at a Brazilian bank.  \par \par \uc2 Exporters want the government to buy dollars to weaken the real and boost the global competitiveness of their products.  \par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has frequently indicated it wants to avoid \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to let the real strengthen and cut inflationary pressure even further.  \par \par \uc2 Tame inflation allowed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to make its first interest rate cut in 17 months this month. More reductions from the current 19.5 percent base rate are expected to boost economic growth.  \par \par \uc2 Stock market bellwether Tele Norte Leste Participacoes closed off 0.71 percent at 36.40 reais.  \par \par \uc2 Sound economic fundamentals have allowed Brazilian stocks and the real to gain markedly despite a bribery scandal that has plagued President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva's government since June. (Additional reporting by Nathalia Ferreira and Juliana Siqueira)  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-BRAZIL (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|U|D|M|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050929e19t001gr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
