\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil stocks end at record close;  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  flat  \b0\par\par\uc2 453 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2005\par 16:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Brazil, Sept 16 (Reuters) - The Bovespa <.BVSP> stock index set historic closing and intraday highs on Friday, with Brazil's risk premium trading at an eight-year low and domestic interest rate cuts spurring hopes of faster growth in South America's largest economy.  \par \par \uc2 The rally meant Brazil joined Mexico and Argentina, where stock market records were broken this week as tame U.S. inflation staves off worries that aggressive U.S. rate rises that could lure money away from emerging markets.  \par \par \uc2 The benchmark index of the Sao Paulo Stock Exchange gained 1.53 percent to finish at 29,815.8 points. It also set a historic intraday peak at 29,863.42, topping record highs set in March.  \par \par \uc2 "Scenarios for the domestic and international economies are positive ... and U.S. rate hikes should continue to be very gradual," said Andre Querne, a fund manager at Maxima Asset Management in Rio de Janeiro.  \par \par \uc2 As the U.S. Federal Reserve hikes rates slowly, on Wednesday Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  trimmed its benchmark rate to 19.5 percent a year. It was the first cut in 17 months and tame inflation makes it likely more will follow.  \par \par \uc2 "Now that the easing cycle has started, the consensus is that we're going to get successive rate cuts, which is a good sign," said Ademir Carvalho, an equities trader at Finabank.  \par \par \uc2 Demand for Brazilian assets is strong, despite a government bribes scandal that has hobbled President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva's administration since June.  \par \par \uc2 J.P. Morgan's country risk premium, which measures the interest rate penalty Brazil must pay to sell bonds globally, fell slightly to 3.63 percentage points. Changes in the premium often drive the direction of stocks.  \par \par \uc2 CVRD , the world's leading producer and exporter of iron ore. led stocks higher for a second straight day after it offered to buy Canadian mining group Canico Resource Corp. for $669 million. CVRD shares rose 4.8 percent to 79.96 reais.  \par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the Brazilian real <BRBY> \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dipped 0.09 percent to end at 2.299 to the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the real rallied nearly 1.4 percent, boosted by heavy inflows of greenbacks from exports and corporate bond sales as well as news the Treasury is planning to launch its first-ever global bond denominated in reais.  \par \par \uc2 But with the real trading close to a 40-month high, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders warned that the likelihood the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market was growing, limiting potential gains.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 BRAZIL\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|U|D|M|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050916e19g00216\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
