\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Argentina Peso, Bonds Stronger As Mood Improves  \b0\par\par\uc2 589 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 August 2005\par 23:33\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    (Updates with information from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  activity) \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--The Argentine peso strengthened modestly Thursday, and it took significant official \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prevent it from rising further as concerns over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's political crisis waned.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Argentine bonds also benefited from the improved mood, rising across the board after a series of declines in preceding trading sessions. This time, the local fixed-income market moved in tandem with the stock market, where the large-cap Merval index was approaching a record Thursday afternoon.  \par \par \uc2 The peso closed at ARS2.9050 to the dollar, slightly stronger than its close of ARS2.9075 Wednesday. This follows a gain of the same magnitude Wednesday after the peso had reached it weakest point in four months on Tuesday when concerns were growing over the regional market fallout from a widening corruption scandal in Brazil.  \par \par \uc2 Daniel Bou Kahir, a trader at Banco de la Pampa, said the real's positive reaction following testimony against Brazilian Finance Minister Antonio Palocci on Thursday by a former aide, meant market participants "no longer saw a reason to hold dollars" against the peso.  \par \par \uc2 Although municipal aide Rogerio Buratti reiterated his accusations that Palocci received kickbacks from private contractors when he was mayor of the southern city of Riberirao Preto in the 1990s, investors were heartened by the absence of documentary proof. At 1850 GMT, the real was at BRL2.4085, considerably stronger than its Wednesday close of BRL2.4525.  \par \par \uc2 Bou Kahir said demand for the peso, which fell in sympathy with the real last week and earlier this week, was evident in some strong volumes of around $180 million traded in the local electronic market. The fact that the exchange rate hardly moved offered strong evidence, he said, of dollar buying by either the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  or state-owned commercial bank Banco de la Nacion.  \par \par \uc2 Later in the day, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it purchased $53 million in the open market, following two days in which it participation in the market was below $6 million.  \par \par \uc2 Bou Kahir added that this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  suggested that authorities have set ARS2.90 to the dollar as the new level to protect. By contrast, he said, there had been little \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the preceding days, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading weaker.  \par \par \uc2 Gains in the bond market were led by the discount bond in pesos. As of late afternoon it was up 2.47% at ARS118.4.  \par \par \uc2 The peso-denominated Bogar 2018, a bond issued as part of the restructuring of provincial debts, was up 1.16% at ARS139.1. Given the apparent preference for longer-dated paper, traders said this longer duration bond may have gone higher if it weren't for news that the government will issue ARS1.8 billion in Bogar 2020 bonds as part of the continued provincial debt refinancing program.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the dollar-denominated Boden 2012 was up 0.47% at a dollar equivalent ARS255.20 and the New York law dollar-based discount bond was unchanged at a dollar equivalent ARS94.3.  \par \par \uc2 Adrian Salvucci, an analyst at Silver Cloud Advisors, said the gain in the fixed-income market suggested an end to the profit-taking that was seen through much of August, as investors shifted into rebounding Argentine stocks.  \par \par \uc2 With both stocks and bonds rising Thursday, "it looks as if valuations have now become attractive," Salvucci said.  \par \par \uc2 -By Michael Casey, Dow Jones Newswires; michael.j.casey@dowjones; 54-11-4313 1918 [ 25-08-05 2133GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050825e18p0010q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
