d fallen in sympathy with the real last week and earlier this week, was evident in some strong volumes of around $180 million traded in the local electronic market. The fact that the exchange rate hardly moved offered strong evidence, he said, of dollar buying by either the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  or state-owned commercial bank Banco de la Nacion.  \par \par \uc2 He added that this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  suggested that the authorities have set ARS2.90 to the dollar as the new level to protect. By contrast, he said, there had been very little \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the preceding days when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading weaker. [ 25-08-05 1907GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Gains in the bond market were led by the discount bond in pesos. As of late afternoon it was up 2.47% at ARS118.4.  \par \par \uc2 The peso-denominated Bogar 2018, a bond issued as part of the restructuring of provincial debts, was up 1.16% at ARS139.1. Given the apparent preference for longer-dated paper, traders said this longer duration bond may have gone higher if it weren't for news that the government will issue ARS1.8 billion in Bogar 2020 bonds as part of the continued provincial debt refinancing program.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the dollar-denominated Boden 2012 was up 0.47% at a dollar equivalent ARS255.20 and the New York law dollar-based discount bond was unchanged at a dollar equivalent ARS94.3.  \par \par \uc2 Adrian Salvucci, an analyst at Silver Cloud Advisors, said the gain in the fixed-income market suggested an end to the profit-taking that was seen through much of August as investors shifted into rebounding Argentine stocks.  \par \par \uc2 With both stocks and bonds rising Thursday, "it looks as if valuations have now become attractive," Salvucci said.  \par \par \uc2 -By Michael Casey, Dow Jones Newswires; michael.j.casey@dowjones; 54-11-4313 1918 [ 25-08-05 1947GM