\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Fitch cuts Brazil bank tied to bribery scandal  \b0\par\par\uc2 524 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juli 2005\par 20:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds comments from Banco Rural, Moody's negative outlook)  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Brazil, July 11 (Reuters) - Fitch Ratings on Monday cut the credit rating of medium-sized Brazilian bank Banco Rural after it was tied to an alleged bribes-for-votes scheme involving the ruling Workers' Party and five of its executives were indicted in a separate case.  \par \par \uc2 Fitch said it cut the bank's long-term, national scale ratings to "BBB-" from "BBB" and signaled another downgrade is possible by revising its outlook to negative.  \par \par \uc2 The ratings agency said the indictment of five executives last week amid a federal investigation into illegal offshore money transfers "may have a relevant impact on the bank's funding, liquidity and ongoing business development."  \par \par \uc2 Federal public prosecutors filed lawsuits against the executives last week.  \par \par \uc2 In a statement, Fitch said: "these rating actions reflect the continued negative impact on the bank's image due to coverage in the press following allegations brought forward against members of Congress that were allegedly receiving improper payments through a scheme operated using current accounts held with Rural."  \par \par \uc2 "The impact on Rural's image was further aggravated by the indictment presented in the Fourth Federal Court in Belo Horizonte against five bank executives last week," Fitch said.  \par \par \uc2 Later on Monday, Moody's Investors Service changed to negative from stable the outlook for Banco Rural's "D-" financial strength rating and "Ba3" rating for long-term local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits in global scale.  \par \par \uc2 "Moody's action reflected the view that the bank may face pressure on its funding base in the wake of recent legal actions involving Rural's \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  and its management team", the agency said in a statement.  \par \par \uc2 Banco Rural said in a statement that Fitch's decision was not based on the quality of its credit portfolio, adding that the bank has "net assets of excellent quality."  \par \par \uc2 The bank also noted an analysis from local ratings agency Austin Rating, saying it had recorded in recent weeks "normal and predictable withdrawals which had not even scratched the bank's financial health."  \par \par \uc2 Banco Rural, according to testimony in Congressional investigations, was the bank from which lawmakers withdrew cash offered by the Workers' Party in exchange for political support.  \par \par \uc2 The bank also loaned 3 million reais ($1.3 million) to the Workers' Party. The party has acknowledged the loan was made but said the money was used for legitimate purposes.  \par \par \uc2 The loan, the party said, was co-signed by Marcos Valerio, the owner of an advertising agency with lucrative government contracts who has been accused of operating the alleged bribery scheme.  \par \par \uc2 The bank has been under stress since the end of last year when \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up Banco Santos, sparking concerns about the financial health of other small financial institutions.  \par \par \uc2 Banco Rural, which is headquartered in Belo Horizonte, the capital of the state of Minas Gerais, has 75 branches in Brazil and net assets of 678 million reais ($288.5 million). ($1=2.35 Brazilian reais)  \par \par \uc2 FINANCIAL-BANCORURAL-FITCH (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050711e17b0028e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
