\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Ends Lower On Ctrl Bk Hints Of  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 406 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Mai 2005\par 22:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA (Dow Jones)--After reaching a three-year high Monday, the Brazilian real weakened against the dollar Tuesday following hints from a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  director that the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  could resume \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in the near future to boost foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 The real ended at BRL2.409 per dollar, compared with BRL2.371 at Monday's close.   \par \par \uc2 Traders said the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slid early in the session after comments by \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monetary Policy Director Rodrigo Azevedo suggesting the bank would extend a program begun last year to bolster reserves.   \par \par \uc2 "Certainly we will return to buying dollars if this doesn't generate volatility," Azevedo said in an address to investment fund managers in Sao Paulo. "Purchases in 2004 and in the beginning of 2005 resulted in an important improvement in the position of foreign reserves. However, this doesn't give a considerable level of comfort."   \par \par \uc2 The real dropped more than 1.0% shortly following the remarks and stayed lower for the remainder of the session.   \par \par \uc2 Azevedo said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has purchased about $10.2 billion so far this year, but noted that net foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows through the end year were projected at $12.3 billion, which would leave a gap of more than $2 billion for possible further purchases to boost reserves.   \par \par \uc2 Brazil's foreign reserves under the international liquidity concept stand at $61.1 billion. Excluding IMF loan funding, however, reserves stand at only around $39.0 billion.   \par \par \uc2 The hints at the possibility of further dollar purchases come as the real has rolled up appreciation of about 10% against the dollar so far this year.   \par \par \uc2 The strong local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has caused increasing discomfort for Brazilian exporters, who despite record-breaking overseas sales have said the appreciation of the real will likely cause negative effects on the trade balance and investment.   \par \par \uc2 Speaking to investors in Europe Tuesday, Brazilian Trade Minister Luiz Fernando Furlan said an ideal level for the real according to local industries would be around BRL2.70 per dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, according to the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  market survey released this week, the real is seen ending June at around BRL2.50 per dollar and dropping to BRL2.70 per dollar by the end of the year.   \par \par \uc2 -By Gerald Jeffris, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-61-8123-6883; gerald.jeffris@dowjones.com [ 31-05-05 2002GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050531e15v000x8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
