\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Brazil Real Opens Down On Higher Inflation Expectations  \b0\par\par\uc2 263 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 2005\par 22:05\par \uc2 OsterDowJones Commodity Wire\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2005, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  Standard Attribution Statement: News Provided by COMTEX.  \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO, May 09, 2005 (ODC via Comtex) --  \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real opened slightly weaker against the U.S. dollar on Monday as traders believe that a rise in inflation expectations, contained in a survey published Monday, will keep \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 The real opened at BRL2.464 per dollar, down from BRL2.462 per dollar from Friday's close, which was the strongest close of the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since May 8, 2002.  \par \par \uc2 Expectations for the IPCA inflation index the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses to guide its monetary policy went up to 6.3% for the end of April from 6.28% a week earlier, according to a survey of more than 100 economists and market analysts polled by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The government's statistics institute is scheduled to announce the IPCA rate for April on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to continue to abstain from \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a stronger real helps to fight inflation.  \par \par \uc2 Continued dollar inflows from exporters, however, are likely to keep the real from weakening much.  \par \par \uc2 Markets also were awaiting a huge foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflow after France's Casino Guichard Perrachon SA (12558.FR) last week raised its stake in Brazil's largest grocer, Companhia Brasileira de Distribuicao SA (CBD), paying EUR407 million to forge a joint venture with CBD's controlling shareholder Abilio Diniz.  \par \par \uc2 -By Bernd Radowitz, Dow Jones Newswires; (55 21) 3288 5004; bernd.radowitz@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires  \par \par \uc2 05-09-05 0922ET  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020050510e159000ij\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
