\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Slips Early As Mkt Awaits Rate Hike, Eyes USD  \b0\par\par\uc2 315 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 2005\par 14:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--Brazil's real traded just a shade weaker early Thursday, as local traders looked to overseas \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets for direction and awaited an expected domestic interest rate hike next week.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  opened at BRL2.703 to the dollar, compared with Wednesday's BRL2.701 close, and continued to hold near that level as the session got under way.  \par \par \uc2 The real has been trading at 2 1/2-year highs near the BRL2.7 level for almost two months as the U.S. dollar plunges against major world \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and strong exports bring in a steady flow of dollars to the local market.  \par \par \uc2 Adding to the real's strength Thursday was the fact that a fifth straight monthly interest rate hike is widely expected from Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  next week. The rate hike, if it comes, will lift Brazil's base rate to a lucrative 18% per year or higher.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Moody's upgrade Wednesday of Brazil's credit rating outlook to positive added to perceptions that more dollars might continue flowing in. If the positive outlook turns to an actual credit upgrade, corporate and government borrowers might float more bonds and debt servicing costs would fall.  \par \par \uc2 But market participants mostly looked to the U.S. Thursday morning, where the release of fresh data on retail sales and unemployment claims could affect the dollar's trajectory.  \par \par \uc2 Traders were also on guard for further \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has entered the market with offers to buy dollars almost daily since the start of December. The dollar purchases have helped the bank build up reserves and also have discouraged bets that the real will continue to gain.  \par \par \uc2 -By Andrea Welsh, Dow Jones Newswires; 5511.3145.1481; andrea.welsh@dowjones.com [ 13-01-05 1340GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1156 1843  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050113e11d000nj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
