\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Opens Little Changed After Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 256 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Dezember 2004\par 21:04\par \uc2 OsterDowJones Commodity Wire\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2004, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  Standard Attribution Statement: News Provided by COMTEX.  \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO, Dec 29, 2004 (ODC via COMTEX) --  \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real opened little changed Wednesday, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market again on Tuesday and revealed that the amount of U.S. dollars it acquired in December so far was higher than most market estimates. The real opened down at 2.693 to the dollar, but then strengthened to Tuesday's close of BRL2.690 again during early morning trading. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday bought an undisclosed amount of dollars at a price of BRL2.690 at a moment when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading little stronger, at BRL2.688 to the dollar. Earlier Tuesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had purchased $2.443 billion dollars in auctions from early December through Monday, more than most market observers had thought, leading many to believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue heavy purchases in the new year. Trading Wednesday also was likely to be influenced by end-of-month trading. Investors typically battle on the last working days of each month to influence the so-called Ptax, or average \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate, for the past calendar month. The Ptax rate will be used to close out dollar futures contracts at the end of the day Thursday. The rate is also used in payment of various other contracts and obligations throughout the Brazilian economy.  \par \par \uc2 -By 