\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Closes Weaker After  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 247 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Dezember 2004\par 20:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real closed slightly weaker Wednesday against the dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 The real closed at BRL2.706 against the dollar, down from Tuesday's close of BRL2.701. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had strengthened slightly earlier in the day, but then fell again after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it offered to buy dollars at a maximum rate of BRL2.698 per dollar, but it didn't reveal the actual amount of dollars it bought.  \par \par \uc2 The purchase came despite comments by Finance Minister Antonio Palocci that the government won't wage a battle to keep the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from gaining too much against the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "The dollar is declining all over the world. We're not so naive as to think Brazil is going to affect the dollar's level worldwide," Palocci said in an interview with the Folha de S. Paulo newspaper published Wednesday. "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is not an option."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  started buying dollars in the market earlier this month, as the real had strengthened beyond BRL2.70 per dollar, threatening to weaken a current export boom.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials have said such purchases are aimed at building the government's foreign reserves.  \par \par \uc2 -By Bernd Radowitz, Dow Jones Newswires; (55 21) 3288 5004; bernd.radowitz@dowjones.com [ 22-12-04 1936GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1156 1843  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020041222e0cm000uk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
