\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's real gains early,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  unlikely.  \b0\par\par\uc2 316 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Dezember 2004\par 14:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Dec 14 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real strengthened early on Tuesday as traders bet Banco do Brasil would soon repatriate 200 million reais in global bonds sold on Monday and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would refrain from buying dollars.  \par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real , gained 0.33 percent to 2.757 per dollar. The Bovespa index of the Sao Paulo Stock Exchange rose 0.54 percent to 25,357 points.  \par \par \uc2 The real is expected to rally on Tuesday, despite caution caused by the Federal Reserve's interest rate meeting and data on the U.S. trade balance in October that could show the country's current account deficit may widen further.  \par \par \uc2 "Overseas bond sales have been expected, along with a possible sovereign sale," Rodrigo Trotta, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the Banif brokerage in Sao Paulo, said. "People are watching closely for the Fed decision and the trade result in the U.S."  \par \par \uc2 With some $50 million in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps maturing in the next session and settling at Tuesday's average trading price, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said it won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when traders jockey to set settlement rates.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy greenbacks to rebuild scant foreign reserves several times since last Monday. Economists have said the plan purchases also help weaken a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that some exporters believe is overvalued.  \par \par \uc2 Despite an expected interest rate hike on Wednesday by Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , stocks were rising early as traders bet falling inflation expectations may convince the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hold rates steady in January instead of hiking them.  \par \par \uc2 Stocks are trying to return to a record high close of 25,632.50 posted last Monday. Bellwether Tele Norte Leste Participacoes (TNLP4.SA), which comprises about 12 percent of the index, rose 0.69 percent early to 42.30 reais.  \par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Nathalia Ferreira).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041214e0ce0094b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
