\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2 , stocks gain after slipping early.   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Terry Wade   \par \uc2 489 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Dezember 2004\par 21:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Brazil, Dec 10 (Reuters) - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stocks recovered from early losses to end higher on Friday, as President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva said two years of strict policies have produced the fastest growth in a decade.   \par \par \uc2 The benchmark Bovespa index of the Sao Paulo Stock Exchange rose 1.66 percent to finish at 24,933.3 points, nearly erasing losses from the previous session.   \par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real, finished 0.18 percent stronger at 2.776 reais per U.S. dollar to close higher for the first time since Monday.   \par \par \uc2 It briefly weakened beyond 2.8 per dollar for the first time in a month as the dollar rallied for a third straight day against the euro and threats of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  limited gains.   \par \par \uc2 Despite a gain for the real, bets the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will gradually weaken encouraged buying of companies that are big exporters. The index is still trying to return to historic highs reached on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 "The real gained today only because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Miriam Tavares, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the AGK brokerage in Sao Paulo, said.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday said it would start buying dollars to rebuild scant foreign reserves. At the same time, the purchases weaken a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that exporters fear is overvalued.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced auctions to buy dollars on Monday, Tuesday and Thursday. It accepted bids in the first two auctions but rejected them in the third.   \par \par \uc2 Still, the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , whether they materialize or not, is limiting would-be gains in a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that gained nearly 5 percent in November on strong dollar inflows from exports and overseas bond sales. \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and rallies by the dollar this week weakened the real nearly 3 percent.   \par \par \uc2 Shares of companies that gain the bulk of their revenues from exports were among the strong gainers as the real looks like it will continue to weaken in the short-term.   \par \par \uc2 Miner CVRD rose 2.41 percent to 57.05 reais, steelmaker Gerdau gained 1.32 percent to 45.19 and jetmaker Embraer finished 3.26 higher at 20.30 reais.   \par \par \uc2 Bovespa bellwether Tele Norte Leste Participacoes, which makes up about 12 percent of the index, dipped 0.22 percent to 41.50 reais.   \par \par \uc2 At a ministerial meeting on Friday, Lula took credit for the strong markets and economy.   \par \par \uc2 "The catastrophe predicted by some never happened," he said.   \par \par \uc2 He said fears his government would adopt inflationary populist policies were misplaced and that the last two years of tight monetary and fiscal policies are producing stable growth.   \par \par \uc2 "GDP grew more than hoped and this isn't an unstable bubble," he said.   \par \par \uc2 Brazil's gross domestic product is expected to surpass 4.6 percent this year, the fastest rate of growth in a decade, and cool next year to 3.5 percent.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041210e0ca00cku\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\