\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil stocks and  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  end down, paring losses.   \b0\par\par\uc2 413 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Dezember 2004\par 21:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Brazil, Dec 8 (Reuters) - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell against the dollar on Wednesday after the weakened greenback partially recovered against the euro, while the stock market cut losses thanks to rising New York bourses.   \par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real , fell 0.44 percent to close at 2.759 reais per U.S. dollar, narrowing losses of more than 1 percent. Meanwhile, the Bovespa index of the Sao Paulo Stock Exchange pared early losses to end 0.08 percent down at 24,968 points. It is struggling to hang onto a record high reached on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 The real slipped even though the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  refrained from buying dollars as it did in the two previous trading sessions. The threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  is checking any would be rallies that \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strong fundamentals warrant, traders said.   \par \par \uc2 "The two \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week were done at rates weaker than where the real was trading. That indicated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't comfortable with the stronger rates and the market responded to this," Jorge Knauer, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Banco Prosper, said.   \par \par \uc2 The real hit a 2-1/2-year closing peak against the dollar on Friday but has been losing ground since Monday when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced it would start buying dollars to rebuild scant foreign reserves and, simultaneously, weaken the real.   \par \par \uc2 Still, the real is more than 3 percent ahead this year after gaining 4.9 percent in November. Exporters fear its strength could hurt \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's competitiveness abroad. Before the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  started, the real was at 2.699 per dollar. A rare rally by the dollar against the euro on Wednesday pressured the real.   \par \par \uc2 Despite a second day of stumbles by electricity generators, telecommunications shares helped lessen the Bovespa's fall.   \par \par \uc2 Stocks in federal power holding Eletrobras (ELET6.SA), one of the main sellers that received low prices for power contracts at a huge auction on Tuesday, fell 11.95 percent to 37.00 reais.   \par \par \uc2 After falling on Tuesday, shares of power distributors that bought cheap electricity contracts at the auction rose. Sao Paulo's distributor Eletropaulo (ELPL4.SA) rose 2.9 percent to 71.00 reais after falling 3.7 percent on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 Among telecoms, which traders say have lagged the index all year, bellwether phone company Tele Norte Leste Participacoes (TNLP4.SA) rose 0.98 percent to 42.30 reais. Telesp Celular (TSPP4.SA) gained 1.04 percent to 6.78 reais.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041208e0c800dql\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
