\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real drops as cenbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2 , stocks ebb.  \b0\par\par\uc2 431 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 2004\par 22:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Dec 7 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars for a second day in a row on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday, sending the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  1 percent lower, and stocks took a blow from low prices at a giant energy auction.  \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real , fell just over 1 percent to 2.747 per U.S. dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars at 2.722 to rebuild foreign reserves.  \par \par \uc2 The real, which hit a 2-1/2-year closing peak against the dollar on Friday, reversed course on Monday sliding 0.37 percent after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced it was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market for the first time since February.  \par \par \uc2 "They are not buying big lots, but their presence inhibits dollar sales. If the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  maintains its stance, the dollar easing trend should be inverted," said Marco Antonio Azevedo, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Brascan bank.  \par \par \uc2 Some government ministers say the real is too strong and could hurt export competitiveness in coming months.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the main Bovespa index of the Sao Paulo Stock Exchange fell 2.5 percent to 24,988 points after failing to hang onto historic highs reached in the previous session as power utilities crumbled.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said lower-than-expected prices for electricity at a groundbreaking power auction caused the power utilities index to drop 4.2 percent as hopes for higher revenues in the sector faded away. The price for 2005 delivery fell to 62 reais by Bovespa's close while the market had expected 70 reais.  \par \par \uc2 Stocks in federal power holding Eletrobras (ELET6.SA), one of the main sellers at the auction, fell 9.2 percent to 42.02 reais. Even shares in power distributors who bought cheap electricity at the auction fell as analysts saw the prices there as bad for investment in the sector.  \par \par \uc2 Sao Paulo's distributor Eletropaulo (ELPL4.SA) fell 3.7 percent to 69 reais.  \par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, shares in telecommunications firm Embratel Participacoes SA (EBTP4.SA) slid 12.6 percent to 5.55 reais after the company said it plans to issue up to 1.9 billion reais ($703 million) in new shares.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts fear Embratel's parent company, Telefonos de Mexico (TMX.N), could use Embratel as a vehicle to finance its pending acquisition of Brazil's Net Servicos de Comunicacao (PLIM4.SA), the debt-laden struggling cable television company, or AT&T Latin America, which Telmex bought in February.  \par \par \uc2 Net's shares ended flat 0.6 reais.  \par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Nathalia Ferreira and Juliana Siqueira).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041207e0c700fth\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
