\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real weakens on renewed cenbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 131 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 2004\par 14:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Dec 7 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars for a second straight day on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday, extending the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall from Friday's 2-1/2-year closing peak.  \par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real , fell 0.22 percent to 2.725 per U.S. dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would snap up greenbacks to rebuild foreign reserves and, in the process, weaken the real.  \par \par \uc2 Some industrialists and economists say the real is too strong and could hurt export competitiveness in coming months.  \par \par \uc2 The main Bovespa index of the Sao Paulo Stock Exchange struggled to hang onto historic highs reached in the previous session and fell 0.03 percent to 25,555 points.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041207e0c7009co\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
