\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil real eases as gov't steps up dollar purchases.   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Terry Wade   \par \uc2 696 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Dezember 2004\par 18:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Brazil, Dec 6 (Reuters) - Brazil intensified its dollar purchases on Monday, weakening its real \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the process while taking advantage of extraordinary \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows to rebuild cash reserves.   \par \par \uc2 Less than two weeks after the Treasury made a similar announcement, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. The unexpected announcement occurred after the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened past 2.70 per dollar to 2.699 earlier on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 After the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the first by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  since February, the real weakened 0.70 percent to 2.728.   \par \par \uc2 Under the rules of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's floating-rate \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime, the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  cannot target a value for the real and can only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if one of the two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market lacks liquidity.   \par \par \uc2 Nonetheless, the purchases on Monday occurred against a backdrop of worries among industrialists that the real, currently at 2-1/2-year highs, is too strong and will hurt the country's record trade surplus in coming months.   \par \par \uc2 "There could be a new floor or a trading band, but we would need to have another strong rally to test this and see at what price the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Jose Roberto Carreira, head \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at the Novacao brokerge in Sao Paulo.   \par \par \uc2 Later on Monday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely disclose the exchange rate at which it purchased dollars, but not the amount bought. Traders said the rate was around 2.715.   \par \par \uc2 Brazil Trade Minister Luiz Fernando Furlan and Agriculture Minister Roberto Rodrigues have sided with industrialists, who are pushing for a weaker real at about three per dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Despite the calls for a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , some economists say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should let the real strengthen in the short term to better contain inflation that is being pressured by high global oil prices.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Treasury officials maintain they have no desired value for the real. The Treasury said less than two weeks ago it earmarked $3.0 billion for spot market purchases through June to pay down foreign debt.   \par \par \uc2 Afonso Bevilaqua, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economic policy director, said Monday's purchases will help rebuild scant foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in January said it would buy dollars this year via spot market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The purchases were curtailed after only one month but are now starting again.   \par \par \uc2 "This continues the plan we announced January 6. We want to rebuild reserves over the medium term without any specific worry about the exchange rate," Bevilaqua said.   \par \par \uc2 According to the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data, Brazil's net foreign reserves are estimated at $24 billion, well below the $70 billion it had before trying unsuccessfully to defend the then fixed-rate real from speculation starting in late 1998.   \par \par \uc2 Including IMF funds, Brazil has $50 billion in reserves, but economists say the country needs to rebuild reserves if it hopes to go it alone without aid from the IMF when its current accord with the lender expires early in 2005.   \par \par \uc2 "This is an atypical period for emerging markets, with huge dollar inflows, so the government has an opportunity to accelerate its dollar purchases," said Mauro Schneider, economist at ING in Sao Paulo.   \par \par \uc2 "This is the correct strategy. I think the Treasury could buy more and do this without implying a desired level for the real," he said.   \par \par \uc2 In the past, the Treasury has bought more than expected. In 2003, it said it would buy around $6 billion on the spot market to fund external debt payments but bought $11.2 billion.   \par \par \uc2 The real is currently trading at its strongest levels since June 2002. It rallied last week on strong economic data, heavy dollar inflows from exports and overseas corporate bond sales, and a dollar that is sliding to record lows against the euro.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts say more \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases may be in store as the only external factor seen causing the real to weaken in the near term would be an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the euro's rally against the dollar. (Additional reporting by Rodrigo Gaier).    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041206e0c6009yk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
