\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real falls after  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes \highlight\uc2 .   \b0\par\par\uc2 364 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Dezember 2004\par 15:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Dec 6 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real fell abruptly against the dollar on Monday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced its first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to purchase dollars since February.   \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slid 0.63 percent to 2.726 to the dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , reversing an earlier gain of 0.37 percent to 2.699. Meanwhile, the Bovespa index of the Sao Paulo Stock Exchange was treading water and virtually unchanged 25,492 points after finishing at a record high on Friday.   \par \par \uc2 "There was no liquidity in the real before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought up all dollars offered at 2.715 but we don't know how much the market offered," Jose Roberto Carreira, head \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at the Novacao brokerage in Sao Paulo, said.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely disclose the exchange rate at which it purchased dollars, but not the amount bought, later on Monday. Traders said the rate will likely be around 2.715.   \par \par \uc2 Under the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rules, it can only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if one of the two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market lacks liquidity.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  follows a government plan announced less than two weeks ago to buy $3 billion on the spot market through June via the Treasury. That plan, the government says, is aimed at paying down foreign debt and rebuilding foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 Economists, however, say both strategies amount to an attempt to weaken the real or stem its appreciation.   \par \par \uc2 The real is trading at its strongest levels in two-and-a-half years. It rallied last week on strong economic data and heavy dollar inflows from exports and overseas corporate bond sales.   \par \par \uc2 But its strength has worried some industrialists who say the real needs to weaken to around three per dollar to keep exports competitive. Some economists, however, say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could better contain inflation expectations if it lets the real strengthen to limit the impact of high global oil prices.   \par \par \uc2 Among individual stocks, Unibanco (UBBR11.SA) fell 1.44 percent to 15.70 after Commerzbank said it would sell its stake of about 5 percent in the Brazilian bank through a secondary share offering.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041206e0c6008qv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
