\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's Real Closes Flat At BRL2.876/Dollar  \b0\par\par\uc2 350 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 April 2004\par 23:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--Brazil's real closed unchanged Tuesday in a light trading session ahead of the Easter holiday, which begins Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The real closed at BRL2.876 to the dollar, the same level as Monday.  \par \par \uc2 There is little in the way of market-moving news expected this week, say traders, who are marking time in a holiday-shortened week. Markets will be closed on Good Friday.  \par \par \uc2 However, some traders are on guard for possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as part of a policy of buying dollars to build up its international reserves. The bank hasn't purchased dollars since February, but some analysts believe that the current dollar exchange rate of under BRL2.9, may tempt the bank to enter the market over the next week or two.  \par \par \uc2 If the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  opts to buy dollars, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to be weakened as more reals will be put into circulation.  \par \par \uc2 The market had been watching for comments from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's head of international affairs, Alexandre Schwartsman, who met with analysts in New York Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Traders wanted to know if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would sell international bonds in April. Last Tuesday, Brazilian Treasury Secretary Joaquim Levy said that the government was considering a sovereign bond offering in overseas markets during April, according to a report that day by the Agencia Estado news agency of Sao Paulo.  \par \par \uc2 However Schwartsman stuck to a review of Brazil's economy during his meeting Tuesday with analysts and didn't mention bond sales, said one analyst who heard Schwartsman speak.  \par \par \uc2 Whatever the case, news about booming exports continues to underpin the real. A growing number of economists and analysts believe that Brazil's trade surplus this year will break last year's $24.8 billion record.  \par \par \uc2 Economic consultancy IDEAglobal said in report Tuesday that it had increased its forecast of the trade surplus to $26 billion from $22.9 billion.  \par \par \uc2 -By Tom Vogel, Dow Jones Newswires; 5511-3145-1480; tom.vogel@dowjones.com [ 04-06-04 1701ET ]  \par \par \uc2 1156 1843  \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020040406e0460003f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
