\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil Central Bank intervention \highlight\uc2  seen on hold.   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Rodrigo Menderico   \par \uc2 520 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 16:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 , March 11 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will probably refrain from buying dollars on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market any time soon unless there is a sharp spike in the value of the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts say.   \par \par \uc2 After buying $2.6 billion from the market through 26 dollar auctions in January, the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  carried out only one such \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  in February and has done none since then.   \par \par \uc2 The bank said this year it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly to boost \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which were seriously depleted in the 1990s when they were used to prop up the real.   \par \par \uc2 But analysts say a political scandal putting pressure on the real and fears that dollar buying could fuel inflation by increasing the amount of reais in circulation are keeping the bank out of the market for now.   \par \par \uc2 The real has depreciated 0.8 percent since mid-February when an aide to President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva's chief of staff was caught on videotape peddling political favors when he was head of the Rio de Janeiro state lottery.   \par \par \uc2 The scandal has kept markets on edge as the government tries to head off a congressional probe.   \par \par \uc2 It would also be counterproductive for the bank to buy dollars now given a raft of upcoming maturities for its domestically traded debt, some of which is tied to the greenback, analysts said.   \par \par \uc2 "It would be odd for the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy (dollars) at a time when it is buying back dollar-denominated debt maturities, which could pressure the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and make those buybacks more expensive," said Eduardo Castro, head of the fixed income department at ABN AMRO Asset Management in Sao Paulo.   \par \par \uc2 Some $4.1 billion in government and private sector debt comes due in March. The government intends to buy back all $2.4 billion of the debt that matures in the month.   \par \par \uc2 "I think the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  changed its strategy and I'm not sure what the new one will be, but I think it will only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again if there are strongly positive flows (in favor of the real)," said Alexandre Vasarhelyi, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at ING Bank in Sao Paulo.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Carlos Cintra, a fixed income manager at Banco Prosper, said he believed the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue buying dollars on the market, but would wait for the political scandal to blow over first so as not to pressure the real too much.   \par \par \uc2 Other specialists said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could wade back into the market if the real strengthened too much.   \par \par \uc2 The real was trading at 2.92 per dollar on Thursday, or about 0.6 percent weaker than where it began the year and 4 percent lower than its strongest close so far this year, at 2.791 on Jan. 12.   \par \par \uc2 "If it hit 2.7 (reais per dollar), it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again because that (exchange rate) would be bad. It would not be good for the trade balance," said Christiani Rinaldim, head analyst at Consultoria Global Invest.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040311e03b002bv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
